# Simplicity

It doesn't need to be too intricate or sophisticated with advanced notations — just get the job done.

- Prefer the smallest correct change over abstractions or clever patterns
- Avoid unnecessary helpers, layers, or generic utilities for one-off use
- Skip advanced notation or heavy architecture unless the task clearly requires it
- Match existing project style rather than introducing new conventions
